From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:07:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: make the flashlight work -- torch LEDs need both a
 chown and a label

The hardware was never the problem: writing 100 to /sys/class/leds/led:torch_0/brightness as root
lights it. Two separate things stopped the camera provider from doing the same.

DAC first. The provider runs as cameraserver (uid 1047) with the camera group, and the kernel leaves
these nodes root:root 0644, so open() for write fails with EACCES. ueventd now chowns brightness on
both torch LEDs to system:camera 0660, the same shape as the backlight rule that already works.

SELinux second, and it would have bitten as soon as DAC stopped. Upstream labels /class/leds as
sysfs_leds, but that is the symlink directory -- opening through it resolves to the real node under
/devices/soc.0/qpnp-flash-led-27, which falls through to generic sysfs. genfs_contexts now labels
the flash-LED device itself, and hal_camera_default gets rw on sysfs_leds, which upstream grants
only to hal_light.

Worth knowing for next time: this failure produces no avc denial at all, because DAC rejects the open
before SELinux is consulted. What the user sees is "Camera 0 is in use" from CameraService, and
dumpsys media.camera simultaneously reporting "Device 0 is closed, no client instance". The honest
clue is one line from the HAL:

  android.hardware.camera.provider@2.4-service: initFlash: Unable to open node
  '/sys/class/leds/led:torch_0/brightness'

CameraFlashlight's own "is in use, cannot set torch mode" never appears, which is what rules out the
stale mOpenedCameraIds path and points at the HAL returning EBUSY instead.
---
 rootdir/ueventd.qcom.rc        | 9 +++++++++
 sepolicy/genfs_contexts        | 6 ++++++
 sepolicy/hal_camera_default.te | 7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/hal_camera_default.te

diff --git a/rootdir/ueventd.qcom.rc b/rootdir/ueventd.qcom.rc
index 8b30c9c..f06ed32 100644
--- a/rootdir/ueventd.qcom.rc
+++ b/rootdir/ueventd.qcom.rc
@@ -228,3 +228,12 @@
 
 # Add device block for FRP
 /dev/block/platform/soc.0/f9824900.sdhci/by-name/config   0660   system     system
+
+# Camera torch (flashlight). The camera provider drives it by writing brightness on these two LEDs,
+# and it runs as cameraserver in the camera group -- so the kernel default of root:root 0644 makes
+# open() for write fail with EACCES before SELinux is ever consulted. The provider then logs
+#   initFlash: Unable to open node '/sys/class/leds/led:torch_0/brightness'
+# and every setTorchMode returns EBUSY, which reaches the user as "Camera 0 is in use" with no avc
+# denial to point at the real cause.
+/sys/devices/soc.0/qpnp-flash-led-27/leds/led:torch_0   brightness   0660   system   camera
+/sys/devices/soc.0/qpnp-flash-led-27/leds/led:torch_1   brightness   0660   system   camera
diff --git a/sepolicy/genfs_contexts b/sepolicy/genfs_contexts
index 77beccb..93e4e7c 100644
--- a/sepolicy/genfs_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/genfs_contexts
@@ -26,3 +26,9 @@ genfscon sysfs /devices/soc.0/fih_battery.84/power_supply/fih_battery   u:object
 genfscon sysfs /devices/soc.0/msm-bcl-15/power_supply/fg_adc            u:object_r:sysfs_battery_supply:s0
 genfscon sysfs /devices/soc.0/qcom,bcl.67/power_supply/bcl              u:object_r:sysfs_battery_supply:s0
 genfscon proc  /sys/vm/swappiness                       u:object_r:proc_swappiness:s0
+
+# The flash/torch LEDs. Upstream labels /class/leds as sysfs_leds, but that is the symlink directory:
+# opening /sys/class/leds/led:torch_0/brightness resolves to the real node under /devices, which
+# falls through to generic sysfs and is not writable by the camera HAL. Label the flash-LED device
+# itself so the write lands on sysfs_leds.
+genfscon sysfs /devices/soc.0/qpnp-flash-led-27          u:object_r:sysfs_leds:s0
diff --git a/sepolicy/hal_camera_default.te b/sepolicy/hal_camera_default.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f643b43
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/hal_camera_default.te
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# The torch is a sysfs LED rather than something the camera HAL reaches through its own device
+# nodes, so it needs explicit access. sysfs_leds is an upstream type (system/sepolicy/public/file.te)
+# and this device's genfs_contexts puts the flash-LED device under it; only hal_light is granted
+# write upstream, which is why the camera provider could not use it.
+allow hal_camera_default sysfs_leds:dir r_dir_perms;
+allow hal_camera_default sysfs_leds:file rw_file_perms;
+allow hal_camera_default sysfs_leds:lnk_file read;
